                <pb facs="0867" n="763" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg763"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.584/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Sweden (Morehead)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-01-07T11:00:00-05:00">January 7, 1933—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Your despatch 620, December 6, 1932. You are authorized to sign convention
                    limited to military obligations. See page 3, lines 3 to 7, Department’s
                    instruction No. 73, September 2, 1931. Full powers by early pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
